   "note": "Design: A translationally invariant ansatz block on a ring topology. The block consists of two layers of entangling CNOTs (0->1, 1->2, ..., 5->0) interleaved with single-qubit RY rotations. Each qubit has its own trainable parameters for the RY gates in both layers (p0-p5 for layer 1, p6-p11 for layer 2). The structure is invariant under cyclic permutations of the qubit indices if the parameters are also permuted cyclically. This symmetry aligns with the likely structure of the input data (6 indexed sites) and the readout observables (Z_i and Z_iZ_j), potentially reducing the effective search space and improving generalization. The use of RY allows for arbitrary single-qubit rotations when combined with the feature map's RZ gates.",
